From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:28:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Create no view of the other type for meta views

Every sampled 2D or 2D array view also gets a Metal view of the other
type, for D3D12 applications that bind one to a declaration of the other.
Mesa's meta operations create views of their own for every blit, clear
and copy, and their shaders declare the type of the view, so the extra
Metal view only cost time while recording.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
index b7c08d7..ae6d6c8 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
@@ -198,9 +198,12 @@ kk_image_view_init(struct kk_device *dev, struct kk_image_view *view,
           * its bloom and tonemapping read as a 2D texture. Other APIs read
           * such a view as its first layer, Metal reads garbage from a texture
           * whose type differs from the declaration. Keep a view of the other
-          * type for the shader to pick by its declaration.
+          * type for the shader to pick by its declaration. Mesa's own meta
+          * shaders declare the type of the view they create.
           */
-         if (view_layout.sample_count_sa <= 1 &&
+         if (!(view->vk.create_flags &
+               VK_IMAGE_VIEW_CREATE_DRIVER_INTERNAL_BIT_MESA) &&
+             view_layout.sample_count_sa <= 1 &&
              (view_layout.view_type == VK_IMAGE_VIEW_TYPE_2D ||
               view_layout.view_type == VK_IMAGE_VIEW_TYPE_2D_ARRAY)) {
             struct kk_view_layout other_layout = view_layout;
